  "body": "Follow-up from #369 (PR #395).\n\n**Today:** the lathe holder judge excludes only the tool's own modelled footprint (the swept insert outline) from the body. A vendor mesh often includes the insert plate beyond the nose circle, so the plate's side edge can be read as rubbing the material the insert is cutting. That errs toward blocking, never toward a gouge. The workaround is to import the holder without the insert.\n\n**Proposed:** an optional insert-zone on the lathe body (a length along the cutting edge, or a box in the tool frame) excluded from the judge. Alternatively, take it from the vendor insert frame once #370 reads the ISO 13399 coordinate systems.\n\n**Done means:** a mesh with its insert plate included, on a plain OD pass, posts clean with the zone set and is refused as today without it.",
